From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 00:51:56 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: apple: t8132-j604: Enable the SIO and the
 HDMI port's audio

The J604's HDMI audio is DPA1, fed by the SIO on channel 0x66. The SIO,
its mailbox and DART, the SIO_CPU and DPA1 power domains and DPA1 were
all disabled, and the board gave the SIO no "sio" alias, so m1n1 never
built its tables.

m1n1 admits the T8132 SIO path for the J604 and builds the protocol-10
tables from the J604's boot ADT, whose SIO firmware is pre-loaded. The
kernel's T8132 SIO driver starts only a protocol-10 firmware. A DP audio
interface linked to a T8132 dcpext binds on its own.

Add the alias, and enable the SIO mailbox, its DART, SIO_CPU, DPA1 and
the DPA1 audio interface. m1n1 enables the SIO node itself once its
tables are in place. Two more changes make it probe:

- The shared T8132 description gives the SIO a 0x88000 coprocessor
  window, which also covers its ASC mailbox at coprocessor + 0x8000.
  The mailbox probes first, so the SIO driver could not request its
  window (-EBUSY). Map 0x8000, as on T6030 and T6041. The driver only
  uses the CPU control register.
- DPA1's parent, DPA_P, was disabled for this board. That was carried
  over from the J713 decision, and the J604 ADT has the domain, on at
  boot. Without it DPA1 waited for a supplier that never registered and
  failed at the deferred probe timeout (-110). Enable it.

Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: LLM
(cherry picked from commit e6b9411499d019f0e34682dd456568bf3b8da0b1)
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi | 36 ++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 32 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
index cb97e5a52b..60e42640a1 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/apple/t8132-j604-lab.dtsi
@@ -19,6 +19,12 @@ aliases {
 		/delete-property/ spmi-primary;
 		/delete-property/ pmu-primary;
 		/delete-property/ nvram;
+		/*
+		 * m1n1 builds the SIO's protocol-10 tables from the J604 ADT,
+		 * reserves its pre-loaded firmware and enables it by this alias
+		 * (T8132_PATH_SIO is admitted for the J604).
+		 */
+		sio = &sio;
 	};
 };
 
@@ -61,7 +67,7 @@ dpaudio1: audio-controller-1 {
 		dmas = <&sio 0x66>;
 		dma-names = "tx";
 		power-domains = <&ps_dpa1>;
-		status = "disabled";
+		status = "okay";
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <0x01>;
 			#size-cells = <0x00>;
@@ -377,8 +383,9 @@ &ps_gfx {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/* J604 ADT: SIO_CPU (pmgr 0x268) under SIO, whose parents have no power register. */
 &ps_sio_cpu {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ps_fpwm0 {
@@ -437,8 +444,12 @@ &ps_uart_p {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * J604 ADT: DPA_P (pmgr 0x2e0) is the parent of DPA0-4 and is on at boot.
+ * DPA1 (the HDMI port's audio) needs it registered as its supplier.
+ */
 &ps_dpa_p {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ps_aes {
@@ -541,8 +552,9 @@ &ps_dpa0 {
 	status = "disabled";
 };
 
+/* J604 ADT: DPA1 (pmgr 0x418) under DPA_P, as the DT describes. */
 &ps_dpa1 {
-	status = "disabled";
+	status = "okay";
 };
 
 &ps_atc0_cio_usb {
@@ -1044,10 +1056,26 @@ &avd_dart {
 	status = "okay";
 };
 
+/*
+ * The ASC mailbox sits at coprocessor + 0x8000, so the coprocessor window
+ * the driver maps stops there, as on T6030 and T6041 (the J604 ADT's 0x88000
+ * covers the mailbox). The driver only uses the CPU control register.
+ */
 &sio {
+	reg = <0x3 0xade00000 0x0 0x8000>,
+	      <0x3 0xad850000 0x0 0x4000>;
 	dma-channels = <0x80>;
 };
 
+/* The SIO's mailbox and DART; the SIO itself is enabled by m1n1 with its tables. */
+&sio_mbox {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
+&dart_sio0 {
+	status = "okay";
+};
+
 &pmgr_cio {
 	status = "okay";
 };
-- 
